{
	"name": "Emperor Porpoise",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>These black and bronze-colored porpoises are sometimes seen along coastlines and in bays, coves, and other sheltered saltwater waterways. Solitary but naturally curious creatures, emperor porpoises will often approach seagoing vessels or individuals swimming in deeper waters. To the unassuming eye, they are simply here to frolic, but observant individuals will realize that the porpoise is enticing them to follow it. Adventurers who succeed on a DC 15 Nature check recognize the cetacean’s intentions and can choose to follow it. The emperor porpoise will lead its follower to treasure, often in the form of a sunken ship or other wreckage.</p>",
